IRWB-022-F is ready for review: [ticket](ttmp/2026/11/26/IRWB-022-F--lowering-tix-to-cuda-checked-on-the-gpu-machine/index.md) · [design](ttmp/2026/11/26/IRWB-022-F--lowering-tix-to-cuda-checked-on-the-gpu-machine/design-doc/01-checked-tix-to-cuda-lowering.md) · [diary](ttmp/2026/11/26/IRWB-022-F--lowering-tix-to-cuda-checked-on-the-gpu-machine/reference/01-implementation-diary.md).

The design emits CUDA directly from the current Tix IR and checks it with a batched differential contract. **No framework changes are proposed:** a local probe confirmed that the existing cross-kind transformation API supports asynchronous checks, verdict replay, and rejection of a changed candidate. The proposed remote-tool change is an opt-in mode that isolates each run’s files while sharing compiled executables across input batches.

The chosen relation is **sampled tolerance against the current revision’s f64 evaluator**. On the GB10, `expf` alone differed bitwise from rounded JS on 9,821 of 32,768 inputs. All probed intrinsic results and the 1,024-term ordered dot product fit the proposed tolerance. Corpus measurements remain for implementation after review.

